Original commit body from f9052277983bc7176f9844132e9d1edba2447ff0:

A pass that FOUND its construct and carried none of it through resolution was
landing in `unreported`, whose declared meaning is that the pass "did not say
why". Those bodies compute the answer and throw it away: the producer helper
returned "" on the branch holding the fact. That is the INV-bikaj complaint one
level down, inside the axis built to cure it.

`candidates_unresolved` is split out of the residue. Both of the helper's
returns are now positive claims, so it is renamed silence_reason_for_candidates.

THE PRIOR RULING IS OVERTURNED, and its three stated grounds were each refuted
by the tree: it called the value "a seventh member" (the vocabulary already held
seven), with "a single producer" (eleven call sites through one helper, the same
shape as no_candidate_construct) and "no consumer" (summarize_silence /
format_silence_summary are vocabulary-generic and wired at cli.py). That last
ground is the one that distinguishes this from prerequisite_absent, which is
still declared with no producer.

MEASURED, twice, not reasoned. The one-line producer change was predicted to
empty `unreported`; it left 2. FOUR return paths never call the helper at all,
and two were firing on this corpus: wasm-bindgen returns early when no Rust
exports exist while its WRAPPER then scans 14 files, and message-dispatch passes
its bail with both sides non-empty and matches no pairs. All four are closed as
a class rather than filed for later. Final distribution:
  no_candidate_files=43, no_candidate_construct=7, candidates_unresolved=4,
  unreported=0

The name describes the PASS, not the repository: ipc rejects some candidates on
a quality filter with no pairing attempted, so a "missing counterpart" name
would be false for it, and a pass cannot tell an absent counterpart from its own
matcher missing one.

STATED HONESTLY: unreported=0 measures the corpus, not completion. 53 of 64
linker modules make no body claim at all. The "size of the remaining work" gloss
is removed from ir.py accordingly.

FILING CORRECTION. This was first written as docs/audits/0019 and the format
validator rejected it: audit_findings._REGISTRIES binds exactly three
registry-backed axes (Edge.edge_type, Symbol.kind, Edge.evidence_type) and
VALID_VERDICTS is a closed frozenset. AnalysisRun.silence_reason is a
lightweight catalog-derived axis and cannot be named in a kind: audit_verdicts
block at all. Filed as ADR-0054, which records the rule that is written nowhere
else: docs/audits/ is for the three registry-backed axes. Note
docs/surveys/python-stdlib-module-io-enumeration.md hit the same validator on
its own first attempt at docs/audits/0019.

